(a) Why is the constructor of Loan not public? What could happen if any class could create a loan?

The constructor of Loan is not public because loans must be created only by Member.borrow().

If any class could create a loan, it could bypass the borrowing rules and create invalid loans.

(b) How does your code guarantee the multiplicity 1.. of the authors of a book? Which multiplicity cannot be guaranteed?*

The Book constructor requires at least one author.

The multiplicity of an Author having at least one Book cannot be guaranteed by the constructor. It can be checked later.

(c) Why do the getters return unmodifiable views of the collections?

To protect the internal collections from modification and preserve the consistency of relationships.

